cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'DMAIC-Bench: From Self-Reflection to Self-Restraint for Agents in Multi-Stage Analytical
  Tasks'
message: If you use this benchmark, please cite it.
type: dataset
abstract: 'A benchmark of self-restraint in multi-stage analytical tasks: whether an agent uses
  the diagnostics it has computed to decide to continue, divert or stop (GO, DIVERT, or NO-GO).
  97 seeded tasks over 15 Lean Six Sigma (DMAIC) cases in four industrial sectors, with paired
  counterfactual variants at the same workflow position, plus a sixteen-task life-sciences extension
  (bulk RNA-seq and case-control GWAS) on the same task contract. Data is released batch by
  batch by a steward that enforces methodological preconditions; the correct route is re-derived
  from seeded data; scoring covers method selection, numeric fidelity and route conformance,
  with blind expert reading of the reports.'
